On Mon, 1 May 2006, Rast wrote:
> Is magenta the same as purple?

As far as nethack is concerned, yes.  It's the only thing remotely close
on the 16-color terminal that Nethack assumes.

> I don't like the idea of shopkeepers being anything other than a nice
> white @.  More generally, displaying peaceful humans as "K" feels wrong.
> You should move those last four items back to "@", and put soldier,
> sergeant, lieutenant, and captain in "K".

"@" is presently no indicator of peace to me.  Grey elves, woodland
elves, soldiers, and lieutentants are always hostile, and take the same
symbol/colors as the watch (before my patch).

My logic is that the shopkeepers, minetown watch, and keystone kops are
basically one team.  If you are indiscreet in acquiring a shopkeeper's
loot, all three will be after you.  Otherwise, the kops will be absent
and the other two will be peaceful.

